# Frozen from tests/push_boundaries.py (tag v0.2.3): inputs as that script generated them, outputs checked once against its Python oracle.
# push on i64/i32/u8/bool (modes 0-3): "checksum requests bytes" equal to the exact growth model through 1M elements.
# Nested arrays (mode 4) and records (mode 5) are stored natively as aggregate blocks: a 32-byte header
# (destructor, stride, element count) before elements of 32 bytes (an array descriptor) or 16 bytes (PushPair).
# They grow by the same rule as modes 0-3: a push reallocates only when header+(n+1)*size exceeds the block's
# power-of-two size class (at least 16 bytes), so pushes are amortised O(1) and a block is less than twice what
# it holds. The script modelled nested arrays with 24-byte elements and no header, and records with one exact
# allocation per push (quadratic bytes); the native layout replaces those constants and the record policy, so
# the expected counters of modes 4 and 5 come from that model with size 32/16 and header 32 through 1M elements (frozen 2026-11-11).
# Build with NEO_ALLOC_STATS=1.
